%% Build order for Contoso backup estate - which decisions are one-way doors, what must be true before the next phase, and where the clocks run
%% Source: codex/playbook-enable-azure-backup-for-file-shares.md Procedure and Steps, codex/blueprint-azure-files-backup-protection.md gate rules; Microsoft Learn "Support matrix for Azure Files backup", "Immutable vault" (WORM region list, locking irreversible), "Multiuser authorization using Resource Guard", "Create and configure Recovery Services vaults" (read 2026-09-03)
timeline
  title Standing up Azure Backup for Azure Files without a one-way door closing behind you
  section Phase 0 - inputs that must exist on paper first
    Records schedule and region : Contoso records-retention schedule per record series, because it sets vault retention and cannot be guessed later : confirm West US is a vault-standard tier region and that cross-region restore is offered there : the vault must be created in the same region as the storage accounts : GATE is a signed retention table and a named second administrator for the Resource Guard
  section Phase 1 - redundancy, the first one-way door
    Vault created empty : New-AzRecoveryServicesVault rsv-contoso-westus : Set-AzRecoveryServicesBackupProperty -BackupStorageRedundancy GeoRedundant : enable cross-region restore now, while zero items are protected : redundancy CANNOT be changed once the first item is protected, so getting this wrong means building a second vault : GATE is storageModelType GeoRedundant and crossRegionRestoreFlag true with an empty item list, recorded in the change ticket
  section Phase 2 - storage account preconditions
    Make the account backup-eligible : allowSharedKeyAccess true, because Azure Backup reads and writes over the key-based data plane : networkRuleSet bypass AzureServices so the trusted-services path survives the firewall lock-down : file share soft delete at 14 days or more : StorageV2 or FileStorage, SMB shares only, NFS cannot be protected : GATE is az storage account show returning true, AzureServices and the vault region
  section Phase 3 - separation of duties before any data exists
    Resource Guard and MUA : the SECURITY admin creates the Resource Guard in a second subscription : the backup admin is granted Reader on it and nothing more : MUA is enabled on the vault and the optional critical operations are kept protected : GATE is a failed attempt - the backup admin tries a protected operation and is refused, and the refusal is filed as evidence
  section Phase 4 - policies sized to the ceilings
    Two policies : AFS-Active-4h-30d-Vault-90d and AFS-Archive-1d-30d-Vault-1y : snapshot retention must respect floor of 200 over the daily snapshot count minus 1, so three snapshots a day allows at most 65 days : the schedule cannot exceed 6 scheduled backups a day : only the last scheduled snapshot of the day transfers to the vault, so a wide window does not buy more vaulted points : GATE is a non-null vaultRetentionPolicy on the active policy
  section Phase 5 - coverage
    Protect every share : File Sync cloud endpoints first : 200 shares per vault per day and 2000 per vault are the ceilings, so a large estate is phased : one on-demand backup per item, 10 on-demand backups per day maximum : GATE is every share from the coverage table Protected and every first job Completed
  section Phase 6 - make failure visible before you trust it
    Alerts and diagnostics : Azure Monitor alerts for all job failures wired to the storage team action group : diagnostic settings for AzureBackupReport, CoreAzureBackup and AddonAzureBackupJobs into Contoso Log Analytics workspace : force a failure by removing the trusted-services bypass on a test account and confirm the mail arrives : GATE is a received alert, not a configured alert
  section Phase 7 - prove recovery before you lock anything
    Restore test : one item-level restore from a snapshot point, and one full-share vault-standard restore to an alternate share with 20 percent headroom : confirm the File Sync servers received the restored paths through change detection : GATE is a job id, a duration, and a matching listing on the server side
  section Phase 8 - immutability, the second one-way door
    Lock only after the restore test : immutability Enabled first, which blocks delete-data, retention reduction and policy downgrade while staying reversible : then Enabled and locked, which is irreversible by design : West US is not yet in the WORM storage GA region list, so a locked vault transitions to WORM automatically when the feature lands, with no data movement and no action : GATE is a documented owner decision, because nobody can undo this later
  section Phase 9 - the replication clock
    Wait out cross-region restore : up to 48 hours after enabling CRR before items appear in the secondary region : then up to 12 hours for each new recovery point to replicate : snapshot-tier points never replicate, so a share on a snapshot-only policy shows no secondary restore points at all : GATE is a listed recovery point in East US, checked and screenshotted, before the engagement closes
